-- chem/cut.cub — the tail of N electrons from the certificate of N−1, by a cut in position (the working state is in the
-- artifact "Exact chemistry from quantum geometry, as proved programs", "The inequality, derived"). The repulsion is
-- diagonal in position, so a cut by position commutes with every potential; only the kinetic energy notices it.
-- (1) Functions J_a of the positions with Σ J_a² = 1. For two of them, J₀ = c, J₁ = s with c² + s² = 1, along one
-- coordinate, with c′ = −k·s and s′ = k·c (k the derivative of the angle; then c″ = −k′s − k²c, s″ = k′c − k²s):
--   c·(cψ)″ + s·(sψ)″ = (c² + s²)·(ψ″ − k²ψ)                                              (`ct-ims`, a polynomial identity)
-- so Σ_a J_a·T·J_a = T + ½Σ_a |∇J_a|² for T = −½Δ, summed over coordinates: H = Σ_a J_a H J_a − ½Σ_a|∇J_a|².
-- (2) Where particle i is the farthest and beyond R, with e the certified lower end of the other N−1 particles'
-- operator, t ≥ 0 its kinetic energy, v ≥ 0 its repulsions and u = 1/r_i ≤ ρ = 1/R:
--   (e + t − Z·u + v) − (e − Z·ρ) = t + v + Z·(ρ − u)                                       (`ct-far`)
-- so that piece is at least e − Z/R. Hence for μ ≤ e − Z/R − C/R² (C/R² ≥ ½Σ|∇J_a|²) the levels of H_N below μ are
-- no more than the levels, below μ + C/R², of H on functions supported in the ball where every particle is near.
-- (3) In the ball r ≤ R′, so ½ω²(r² − R′²) ≤ 0 may be added (`ct-ball`: its value is ½ω²(r − R′)(r + R′)); and
-- θ·T − Z/r = θ·(T − (Z/θ)/r) ≥ θ·(−(Z/θ)²/2) = −Z²/(2θ), hydrogen's lowest level at charge Z/θ (`ct-hyd`); so each
-- particle's h ≥ (1−θ)T + ½ω²r² − ½ω²R′² − Z²/(2θ), and (1−θ)(T + ½Ω²r²) with Ω² = ω²/(1−θ) is (1−θ)T + ½ω²r²
-- (`ct-osc`): a harmonic oscillator, levels (1−θ)Ω(n + 3/2), diagonal in its own shells, so every state with a
-- particle above shell n lies above any chosen number once n is large: the tail constant of chem/tailblock.cub
-- for the span of shells ≤ n. Taken here, not proved: Leibniz's rule in several variables and the sum over
-- coordinates; the hypothesis H_{N−1} ≥ e; that a compression has no more levels below a number than the operator
-- it compresses; hydrogen's lowest level and the oscillator's levels; the existence of the J_a with the bound C/R².
import "tailblock.hypercubical"

